#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:184
msgid "The <strong>Will this ad show?</strong> box on each ad lists everything that could stop it: missing Publisher ID or slot, schedule, targeting, placement."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:185
msgid "Add an ad unit"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:189
msgid "Block, widget & shortcodes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:191
msgid "<strong>Block:</strong> add the \"AdFlow Ad\" block in the editor and pick an ad unit. <strong>Widget:</strong> Appearance → Widgets → \"AdFlow\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:193
msgid "Shortcodes from earlier versions keep working:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:195
msgid "Optional attributes: <code>style</code> and <code>class</code>."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:199
msgid "Automatic placements"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:201
msgid "Placements insert an ad unit into every post without editing posts: <strong>before content</strong>, <strong>after paragraph N</strong> and <strong>after content</strong>, for the post types you choose. Posts shorter than N paragraphs are skipped."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:202
msgid "Put a rotation group in a placement to rotate several ads in the same spot."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:203
msgid "Open Placements"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:207
msgid "More placements: mid-article, between posts, sticky, popup, WooCommerce"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:211
msgid "<strong>Middle of the article (after X%)</strong> - scales with post length."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:212
msgid "<strong>Between posts</strong> - every N posts on home, category, tag and search pages (classic and block themes)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:213
msgid "<strong>Before comments</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:214
msgid "<strong>Sticky anchor</strong> - a closable bar at the bottom; page content is padded so the ad never covers it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:215
msgid "<strong>Popup</strong> - for sponsor banners and other networks, after a delay or scroll depth, once per visitor per N days. Google does not allow AdSense in popups, so AdSense units are never shown there."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:216
msgid "<strong>WooCommerce</strong> - above the product grid, below the product summary, after add-to-cart."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:218
msgid "<strong>Sticky sidebar:</strong> turn on \"Keep in view while scrolling\" on an ad unit and place it last in your sidebar. On desktop it stays visible while visitors read."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:222
msgid "Targeting, scheduling & A/B tests"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:225
msgid "Each placement can be limited by <strong>device</strong> (mobile/desktop), <strong>visitor</strong> (logged in/out), <strong>traffic source</strong> (search engines or not), <strong>categories</strong>, <strong>post age</strong> and <strong>start/end dates</strong>. Device and traffic rules run in the browser, so they work with page caching - and an ad that should not show never requests an ad from Google."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:226
msgid "<strong>A/B rotation:</strong> add extra ad units to a placement; the Earnings screen shows which one earns more."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:227
msgid "<strong>Per post:</strong> the \"AdFlow Ads\" box in the post editor turns off all ads, or only Auto Ads, on that post."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:231
msgid "Google Ad Manager (GPT) units"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:234
msgid "Choose the type \"Google Ad Manager (GPT)\" and enter the <strong>ad unit path</strong> (<code>/1234567/sidebar</code>, from Ad Manager → Inventory → Ad units → Tags), the <strong>sizes</strong> (<code>300x250, 336x280, fluid</code>) and optional <strong>mobile sizes</strong> for screens under 768px."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:235
msgid "<strong>Key-values</strong> (one <code>key=value</code> per line) target line items. Macros: <code>{post_id}</code>, <code>{post_type}</code>, <code>{category}</code>, <code>{placement}</code>."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:237
msgid "GPT loads once, asynchronously, only on pages that show such a unit. Whether a slot fills depends on your line items."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:242
msgid "Your own ads & selling"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:244
msgid "Banners, text ads and custom code"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:246
msgid "Run sponsor, affiliate or house ads next to AdSense. Image banners come from the Media Library; text ads have a headline, text and button. Links get <code>rel=\"sponsored\"</code> (add nofollow if you like) and can open in a new tab."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:248
msgid "<strong>Disclosure label:</strong> \"Sponsored\" or \"Advertisement\" above the ad - laws in many countries require it for paid ads."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:249
msgid "<strong>Schedule:</strong> start and end date and time (your site's time zone). Outside it the ad hides itself, even on cached pages."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:250
msgid "<strong>When not running:</strong> show an AdSense unit instead, so the space keeps earning."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:251
msgid "Own ads use neutral class names, so ad blockers are less likely to hide them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:253
msgid "Destination links may contain tracking macros: <code>{ad_id}</code>, <code>{placement}</code>, <code>{site}</code>, <code>{cachebuster}</code>."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:257
msgid "Rotation groups"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:259
msgid "A rotation group shows one of its ads per page view: <strong>weighted</strong> (an ad with weight 3 shows three times as often as weight 1) or <strong>in order</strong>. The choice is made in the browser, so it works with page caching."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:260
msgid "Only ads that may show right now take part: scheduled, capped, out-of-hours or other-country ads are skipped. Mix sponsor ads with an AdSense unit so the spot is never empty."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:264
msgid "Sell ads directly (self-serve)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:268
msgid "Create a rotation group (Ad Units → Add → Rotation group) and put it in a placement."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:269
msgid "Under <strong>Settings → Sell ads</strong>, add a package: name, banner or text, size, days, price and your payment link (a Stripe Payment Link, PayPal.me or any checkout)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:270
msgid "Create an \"Advertise with us\" page with the shortcode <code>[adflow_advertise]</code>."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:271
msgid "Advertisers choose a package, upload their banner or write a text ad, and pay with your link (the order number is passed as <code>?order=</code>)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:272
msgid "Orders wait under <strong>Ad Units → Pending</strong>. Check the creative and payment (\"Mark as paid\"), then Publish: the ad joins the package's group for the paid days and stops by itself. The advertiser receives a live report link and weekly emails."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:274
msgid "No card data ever reaches your site. The form works on cached pages and is protected against spam."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:278
msgid "Advertiser reports, emails & pricing"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:282
msgid "<strong>Advertiser details & campaign price</strong> on each own ad; the sponsor eCPM is shown next to your AdSense RPM."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:283
msgid "<strong>Report link:</strong> a read-only page with the ad's statistics - no login. Create or turn it off in the ad's sidebar."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:284
msgid "<strong>Performance emails:</strong> weekly (Mondays) or monthly (the 1st) to the advertiser. \"Email me a preview\" shows what they get."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:285
msgid "<strong>Expiry reminders</strong> to you (and optionally the advertiser) 7 days before and when a campaign ends."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:286
msgid "<strong>Frequency cap</strong> (impressions per visitor per day) and <strong>dayparting</strong> (days and hours)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:287
msgid "<strong>Country targeting:</strong> \"Only in\" or \"Everywhere except\" a list of country codes. The country comes from Cloudflare or your host, or from the optional free country database (Countries field → \"Use the free country database\")."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:293
msgid "Reports & earnings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:295
msgid "How statistics are counted"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:297
msgid "AdFlow counts impressions, viewable impressions and clicks of your own ads using industry (IAB/MRC) definitions:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:299
msgid "<strong>Impression</strong> - the ad was actually displayed (for banners: the image loaded). Hidden, prefetched and prerendered pages do not count."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:300
msgid "<strong>Viewable</strong> - at least half of the ad was on screen for one continuous second."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:301
msgid "<strong>Click</strong> - a link in the ad was opened; a scroll that starts on the ad is not a click."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:302
msgid "<strong>Not counted</strong> - bots, headless browsers, link previews and logged-in administrators."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:304
msgid "It is cookieless: only daily totals are stored - no IP addresses or visitor IDs - and it works with page caching. Under Settings → Tracking you can wait for statistics consent, count clicks through a redirect link instead, and choose how long data is kept."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:305
msgid "AdSense statistics come from Google; AdFlow does not count AdSense impressions itself."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:306
msgid "Open Reports"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:306
msgid "Tracking settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:310
msgid "Full reports, CSV, REST API & WP-CLI"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:313
msgid "Custom date ranges, breakdowns by placement, device and advertiser, and CSV export on the Reports screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:315
msgid "Authenticate the REST API with an Application Password (Users → Profile) of a user who may view reports."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:319
#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-upsell.php:146
msgid "AdSense earnings in WordPress"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:322
msgid "Connect your Google account under <strong>AdFlow → Earnings</strong> to see today, yesterday, this month, page RPM, clicks, top pages and per-unit earnings - plus a dashboard widget. AdFlow only asks for read-only access to AdSense reports."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:327
msgid "Privacy, safety & team"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:329
msgid "GDPR: Consent Mode v2 & loading ads after consent"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:331
msgid "Google requires consent before personalised ads in the EEA, UK and Switzerland. Show the consent message with AdSense's own \"Privacy & messaging\" (a Google-certified TCF message) or a consent plugin such as Complianz, CookieYes or Cookiebot. Then, under <strong>Settings → Privacy & consent</strong>:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:333
msgid "<strong>Load ads after consent</strong> - AdSense, other networks' code and Ad Manager slots wait until the consent tool has answered. Your own banners and text ads use no cookies and show straight away."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:334
msgid "<strong>Google Consent Mode v2</strong> - tells Google tags consent is \"denied\" until the visitor agrees and passes on their choice (read from the WP Consent API). Use it when your banner is not a Google-certified TCF message, and turn it on in only one place."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:336
msgid "Open Privacy & consent"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:340
msgid "Invalid-click protection & ad limits"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:343
msgid "Stops showing ads to a visitor who clicks ads too often (e.g. 3 clicks in 24 hours → no ads for 7 days). Flagged visitors never load the AdSense script, so no ad is ever hidden - hiding ads breaks AdSense policy. It reduces risk; no tool can guarantee Google's decisions."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:344
msgid "Also on Settings → Click protection: <strong>max ads per page</strong> and a polite <strong>ad-blocker message</strong>. Settings → Performance: <strong>lazy loading</strong>; each ad unit: <strong>reserved height</strong> against layout shift."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:348
msgid "Roles, permissions & approvals"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:350
msgid "Under <strong>Settings → Access</strong>, give other roles \"Create & edit ads\", \"Publish ads (no review)\" and \"View reports\". Administrators always have full access; settings stay with administrators."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:351
msgid "<strong>Approval workflow:</strong> someone who may create but not publish ads gets \"Submit for Review\". Everyone who may publish is emailed, and the Dashboard shows the ads waiting."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:352
msgid "Open Access"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:356
msgid "Activity log"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:359
msgid "Who created, changed or deleted which ad, placement or setting, and when - under Settings → Activity log."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:364
msgid "Switching & moving"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:366
msgid "Switch from Advanced Ads, Ad Inserter, AdRotate or WP QUADS"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:369
msgid "Open <strong>Settings → Switch to AdFlow</strong>. AdFlow shows what it found - the other plugin does not have to be active."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:370
msgid "Click <strong>Import</strong>. Ads, rotation groups, placements and (AdRotate / WP QUADS) statistics are copied; nothing in the other plugin is changed. Importing again never creates duplicates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:371
msgid "Review the report: AdSense code for your Publisher ID becomes a native AdSense unit, linked banners become image ads, everything else is kept as custom code so it looks exactly as before."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:372
msgid "Deactivate the old plugin. Its shortcodes - <code>[the_ad]</code>, <code>[adinserter]</code>, <code>[adrotate]</code>, <code>[quads]</code> - keep working through AdFlow."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:374
msgid "Open Switch to AdFlow"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:378
#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-upsell.php:731
msgid "Export / import between sites"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:381
msgid "Settings → Import / Export downloads your whole setup (settings, placements, ads.txt, ad units) as one file and restores it on another site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:388
msgid "Ads are not showing"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:391
msgid "Look at the <strong>Dashboard</strong> checks and the ad's <strong>Will this ad show?</strong> box."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:392
msgid "Open a page while logged in and choose <strong>AdFlow → Inspect ads on this page</strong> in the toolbar: every ad is outlined as filled, unfilled or blocked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:393
msgid "\"Hide ads for administrators\" (Settings → General) hides ads from you - check in a private window."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:394
msgid "Purge your cache plugin, and exclude <code>adsbygoogle.js</code> from JavaScript \"delay\" or \"combine\" features."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:395
msgid "With \"Load ads after consent\" on, ads wait for the consent banner to be answered."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:396
msgid "Unfilled AdSense spaces are Google's decision (new site, low traffic, policy). They are not an AdFlow error."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:401
msgid "Your data, updates & uninstalling"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:403
msgid "Updating never changes how existing ads look; new features start switched off. Deleting the plugin keeps your ads and settings unless you turn on \"Also delete all AdFlow ads, settings and statistics\" under Settings → General → Your data."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:407
msgid "Installing Pro & your license"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:411
msgid "Keep the free AdFlow plugin active - Pro is an add-on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:412
msgid "Upload adflow-pro.zip under Plugins → Add New → Upload Plugin and activate it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:413
msgid "Enter your key under Settings → License to receive updates and support. Pro features keep working if a license expires."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:418
msgid "For developers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:420
msgid "Useful filters and actions:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:422
msgid "<code>adflow_should_display_ad</code> ($display, $unit, $context) - hide a particular ad."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:423
msgid "<code>adflow_ads_allowed</code> - turn all ads off on a request."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:424
msgid "<code>adflow_ad_markup</code> ($html, $unit, $context) - change the output."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:425
msgid "<code>adflow_ad_wrapper_attributes</code> - add attributes to the ad wrapper."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:426
msgid "<code>adflow_placement_types</code> - register a placement."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:427
msgid "<code>adflow_ad_types</code> + <code>adflow_render_ad_type</code> - register an ad unit type."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:428
msgid "<code>adflow_review_recipients</code> - who is emailed about ads waiting for review."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:429
msgid "<code>adflow_imported</code> - runs after an import from another plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:430
msgid "<code>adflow_geo_country</code> (Pro) - supply the visitor country from your own lookup."
msgstr ""

